"""Render the exact three-copy PPT exclusion for N17, t5."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re,hashlib
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def m(x,display=True):
 tag='div' if display else 'span';return f'<{tag} class="math" data-display="{str(display).lower()}" data-tex="{html.escape(x,quote=True)}"></{tag}>'
def links(items):return '<div class="proof-links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{html.escape(u,quote=True)}">{t} ↗</a>' for u,t in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 r=json.loads((HERE/'independent-verification.json').read_text());assert r['passed'] and r['n']==17 and r['t']==5
 assert r['certificateSHA256']==hashlib.sha256((HERE/'certificate.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-qec-upper/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)+'\n.math{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}.proof-step{border-left:3px solid #b8c9bd;padding-left:1.2rem;margin:2rem 0}.badge{color:#1c6253;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em}'
 b='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent states and subspaces · Exact exclusion</p><a href="../../index.html#n=17&t=5">← Catalogue entry</a><h1>Seventeen qubits have maximum AC order four</h1>'
 b+='<div class="result"><span class="badge">Proved · arbitrary complex pure states</span>'+m(r'\boxed{K(17,t)=0\quad(t\ge5),\qquad t_{\max}(17)=4.}')+'<p>An exact three-copy certificate excludes every fifth-order AC state. The analytical fourth-order representative in the AC-state catalogue supplies the matching existence result. Sixth and higher orders are excluded by nesting.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>What the AC-state catalogue establishes</h2><p>The catalogue contains a normalized six-component radical state with</p>'+m(r'\rho_4=I_5/5,\qquad \operatorname{Tr}(\rho_5^2)=\frac16+\frac{19}{21658}.')+'<p>This shows that the displayed state has exactly order four. The exclusion below proves that no different fifth-order state exists either. The Liège library and supplied Julia source report an order-four representative at this size; their absence of higher-order examples is not used as a proof.</p>'+links([('../n17-t4/index.html','Exact fourth-order state and coefficients'),('../../../anticoherent-state-catalogue/index.html#n=17&t=4','Pure AC-state catalogue')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>The fifth-order exclusion</h2><div class="proof-step"><h3>1. Average three copies over rotations</h3><p>A hypothetical fifth-order AC state produces</p>'+m(r'X=\int_{\mathrm{SU}(2)}U_g^{\otimes3}(|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|)^{\otimes3}U_g^{\dagger\otimes3}\,dg,\qquad X\succeq0,\quad\operatorname{Tr}X=1.')+'<p>The moment lies on '+m(r'\operatorname{Sym}^3(V_{17/2})',False)+', of dimension 1140. Its low-rank multipoles impose</p>'+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}_1[(T_{\ell0}\otimes I^{\otimes2})X]=0,\qquad\ell=1,\ldots,5.')+'<p>The certificate selects 62 necessary equations on 72 real invariant coordinates. Every equation is reconstructed directly from the physical tensor words.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>2. The partial transpose must also be positive</h3><p>Every integrand is a product projector across the first copy and the other two, so '+m(r'X^{\Gamma_1}\succeq0',False)+'. Conjugating the first factor by spin flip gives a positive invariant operator on '+m(r'V_{17/2}\otimes\operatorname{Sym}^2(V_{17/2})',False)+', of dimension 3078.</p><p>The complete decompositions give 24 positive input coefficient matrices and 26 positive output compressions. Denote the certificate’s dyadically rescaled input matrices by '+m(r'x_J',False)+' and its output compressions by '+m(r'Y_L',False)+'. All are positive semidefinite. Taking real parts preserves the constraints and both positivity conditions, so the argument covers arbitrary complex amplitudes.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>3. An exact separating identity</h3><p>A rational combination of the contraction equations yields</p>'+m(r'0=\operatorname{Tr}X+\sum_J\operatorname{Tr}(C_Jx_J)+\sum_L\operatorname{Tr}(Q_LY_L),\qquad C_J\succ0,\quad Q_L\succ0.')+'<p>The right side is at least one, which is impossible. Exact rational LDL decompositions certify 45 positive input pivots and 126 positive output pivots. Neither a numerical tolerance nor a restricted symmetry ansatz is used in the final proof.</p></div>'+links([('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Exact rational certificate'),('verify_independently.py','Independent standard-library verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Successful exact verification')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>An independent short proof at sixth order</h2><p>Sixth order also admits a rank-one-complement argument: a hypothetical state would force a pure sixth-order AC state on fifteen qubits, contradicting tensor dimension counting. It is a special case of</p>'+m(r'\boxed{K((r+1)^2+1,2r)=0\qquad(r\ge1).}')+links([('../n17-t6/index.html','Short proof and general family of exclusions')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Reproducibility</h2><p>The independent verifier rebuilds all 62 contraction equations, all 72 partial-transpose functional coefficients and every exact positivity factorization. Separate controls check the transformation on arbitrary complex product states and known fourth- and fifth-order witnesses.</p><pre><code>python3 verify_independently.py</code></pre>'+links([('positive-control.json','Physical-map and known-state controls'),('../../index.html#n=17&t=5','Updated subspace catalogue')])+'</section>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>N=17: fifth-order anticoherence is impossible</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+b+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
